course: dictionary
lesson: 11822
title: Words for life on Earth
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A biosphere is the part of Earth where living things exist. Break the word into two parts: bio means life, and sphere means a round shape. «Scientists found plastic in the deep sea, high mountain lakes and even the air, which shows how far pollution spreads through the biosphere.» The clues are deep sea, mountain lakes and air. They show that the biosphere covers every place where life is found.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «...which shows how far pollution spreads through all the places where living things exist.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Words can also have more than one meaning. «The class visited Biosphere 2, a huge closed building that copies natural habitats.» Here the clues are building and copies habitats, so biosphere means a building, not the whole Earth. Always read the sentence to find out which meaning is used.
fact: Biosphere means all the parts of the Earth where living things exist, from deep in the sea to high in the air.
fact: In science, the Earth is described in spheres: atmosphere (air), hydrosphere (water), lithosphere (rock) and biosphere (life).
fact: «Biosphere» can also mean a large closed building made to hold living things and copy natural habitats, such as Biosphere 2 in Arizona.
fact: A biosphere reserve is a protected area where people and nature live together.
fact: Pollution and climate change affect the whole biosphere, not just one small part of it.
exercise: «Pollution can travel across the biosphere, from the deepest sea to the highest air.» What is the biosphere? | A kind of cloud made of dust | A layer of rock deep under the ground | A large glass building for plants | *All the parts of the Earth where living things exist
exercise: In geography, Earth is described in spheres. Which sphere means the air? | Biosphere | *Atmosphere | Lithosphere | Hydrosphere
exercise: «Biosphere 2 in Arizona is a huge closed building where scientists copied natural habitats.» What kind of thing is Biosphere 2? | *A large closed building that holds living things | A weather map | A type of rock found in the sea | A protected park for birds
test: «Clean rivers and healthy forests help keep the biosphere safe.» What does the biosphere include? | *All the places where living things exist | Only the air | Only the sea | Only the land
test: UNESCO names some areas as biosphere reserves. What is a biosphere reserve? | A deep hole in the rock | A factory that makes clean air | *A protected area where people and nature live together | A shop that sells plants
exam: Why might a scientist say that pollution affects the whole biosphere? | It makes the weather sunnier | *It can harm living things everywhere on Earth, from the sea to the sky | It only changes the rocks | It stays in one small pond
